{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Zope Foundation and contributors <zope-dev@zope.dev>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": ["Development Status :: 6 - Mature", "Environment :: Web Environment", "Framework :: Zope", "Framework :: Zope :: 5", "Framework :: Zope :: 6", "Operating System :: OS Independent", "Programming Language :: Python", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.15", "Programming Language :: Python :: Implementation :: CPython", "Programming Language :: Python :: Implementation :: PyPy", "Topic :: System :: Systems Administration :: Authentication/Directory :: LDAP"], "description": "Overview\n========\n\nAuthEncoding is a framework for handling LDAP style password hashes.\n\nIt is used in Zope but does not depend on any other Zope package.\n\nChangelog\n=========\n\n6.1 (2026-09-17)\n----------------\n\n- Move package metadata from setup.py to pyproject.toml.\n\n- Add support for Python 3.14 and 3.15.\n\n- Drop support for Python 3.9.\n\n- Fix tests for newer ``bcrypt`` versions.\n\n\n6.0 (2024-02-26)\n----------------\n\n- Add support for letters that are not part of the latin-1 character set.\n  (`#17 <https://github.com/zopefoundation/AuthEncoding/issues/17>`_)\n\n- Add preliminary support for Python 3.14.\n\n- Add support for Python 3.12 and 3.13.\n\n- Drop support for Python 3.7 and 3.8.\n\n\n5.0 (2023-01-12)\n----------------\n\n- Fix schema sorting bug.\n\n- Drop support for Python 2.7, 3.5, 3.6.\n\n- Add support for Python 3.10 and 3.11.\n\n\n4.3 (2021-06-29)\n----------------\n\n- Replace hand-rolled salt creation with ``os.urandom``\n  (`#8 <https://github.com/zopefoundation/AuthEncoding/issues/8>`_).\n\n\n4.2.1 (2021-04-08)\n------------------\n\n- Test on GHA.\n\n- Skip some tests for broken crypt implementations.\n\n\n4.2 (2020-09-30)\n----------------\n\n- Add support for Python 3.8 and 3.9.\n\n\n4.1 (2018-10-30)\n----------------\n\n- Add support for Python 3.6, 3.7 and PyPy3.\n\n- Drop support for Python 2.6, 3.3 and 3.4.\n\n- Add ``BCRYPTHashingScheme``, optionally available if package is\n  installed with the `bcrypt` extra.\n\n- Accept bytes as input to ``AuthEncoding.is_encrypted``.\n\n\n4.0.0 (2015-09-30)\n------------------\n\n- Supporting Python 3.3 up to 3.5 and PyPy2.\n\n- Added ``SHA256DigestScheme``.\n\n\n3.0.0 (2015-09-28)\n------------------\n\n- Extracted from ``AccessControl 3.0.11``\n", "description_content_type": "text/x-rst", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": ["License-File"], "home_page": null, "keywords": null, "license": null, "license_expression": "ZPL-2.1", "license_files": ["LICENSE.txt"], "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": "Plone Foundation and contributors <zope-dev@zope.dev>", "name": "AuthEncoding", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/AuthEncoding/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/AuthEncoding/", "project_urls": {"Issues": "https://github.com/zopefoundation/AuthEncoding/issues", "Source": "https://github.com/zopefoundation/AuthEncoding"}, "provides_extra": ["test", "bcrypt"], "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/AuthEncoding/6.1/", "requires_dist": ["pytest; extra == \"test\"", "bcrypt; extra == \"bcrypt\""], "requires_python": ">=3.10", "summary": "Framework for handling LDAP style password hashes.", "version": "6.1", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "releases": {"5.0": [{"comment_text": "", "core-metadata": {"sha256": "4ba4c23182be750fa4954362db64de4ec79b882aedcfca651162600957b09e37"}, "digests": {"blake2b_256": "95bd5d09fb6cdd06203e9e43feb23a0f29030e373e4672af116e5195b83e9d13", "md5": "751bc04f571b12ee22919d0843af9b22", "sha256": "1a66fb53801d10b15455c9494e97ada3d2e92a408749ec519bc8